  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat proved itself to be a social platform/network of a new generation, and, as you may know, people tend to refer to their VRC username almost like a visiting/business card quite often. So, what I'm trying to say is, it would be nice if VRChat's website would let users share their profile with specific details they'd like to share, similarly to the traditional social networks used to this day. \nIt's useful not only for social purposes, which may be already more than common enough for someone to make the post you're reading right now, but also to show off people's professional skills by presenting their VRChat projects, which is what I did while I was looking for a job, and yet most recruiters didn't bother visiting my worlds because the website either seems uncomfortable or doesn't provide them with enough details to prove that the user in question actually worked on the project they're presenting. \nI'm talking about the possibilities of business with VRChat users because this is what let me get a decent job as a level designer, and I'd like to see if VRChat is willing to make their website more accessible to people outside of their own user base in order to let people who use VRChat get something useful in return for their hard work, as well as the ability to socialize, which is probably what the app has always been intended to be used for.",
